 {"id": "BT-077", "title": "P2 — track multiple associated PRs, branches, and worktrees on a task so related work artifacts are not lost", "priority": "P2", "status": "complete", "reasoning": "Bane 2026-10-05: tasks should be able to record a set of related PRs and, similarly, multiple branches and worktrees across the dimensions involved in the task. Agents need to find what they are working on or what is associated with the work, rather than losing the relationship when a task spans several worktrees/branches/PRs. Design additive structured plural fields (e.g. pull_requests, branches, worktrees or a validated association object), preserving existing singular worktree/branch fields and sessions for backward compatibility. Support create/update/read/validate/render/export round-trip; preserve all associations when one is added or removed; expose them in list/show/search/result sets; validate element types and reject malformed values. Include tests for multiple values per dimension, legacy singular rows, merging/adding associations without overwriting siblings, and PR URL/number identity normalization rules.", "capability_tags": [], "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "001c75e", "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": "feat: plural association fields (pull_requests/branches/worktrees) with PR URL/number normalization, merge-without-overwrite per dimension, legacy singular-row compat, create/update/show/list/search/render/export round-trip. Worker gates green (build/vet/test/gofmt); foreman re-ran full go build/vet/test green + guard PASS; CLI probes on throwaway board: 2 PRs+2 branches+2 worktrees accumulate, 3rd PR merge preserves siblings, malformed rejected exit 1, legacy row renders; validate+doctor OK on live board (read-only).", "foreman_note": null, "completed_at": "2026-10-07T19:14:55.000Z", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-05T15:39:50.5615+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-05T15:39:50.5615+00:0