 {"id": "BT-078", "title": "P1 — discover and read symlinked sub-repository boards from a local umbrella repo for a unified cross-repo work view", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "reasoning": "Bane 2026-10-05: multi-service products often use an umbrella repo with submodules/sub-repos; unlike a monorepo, the full work picture spans multiple project boards. The umbrella repo should be able to hold explicit symlinks to each child repo’s .coding-hermes directory, and boardctl (plus a stable library/result surface for future tools) should read the linked boards together so agents can understand related work and cross-repo alignment. Existing BT-021 handles uploaded folders/zips and is not this local workspace-discovery feature. Define/document the explicit symlink registry convention; discover linked boards deterministically; retain source repo/board provenance in every result; handle duplicate task IDs with an unambiguous repo-qualified identity and resolve cross-board relationships without silently binding to the wrong task; support unified list/search/stats/validation results while preserving single-repo -C behavior. Read aggregation must not write through child-board symlinks; writes must be explicitly targeted to one owning repo. Validate symlink target shape, canonicalize targets, dedupe aliases, report broken/looping/unsafe links, and bound traversal (never recursively follow arbitrary symlinks). Add temp-fixture end-to-end tests with at least two child repos, colliding task IDs, a cross-repo task relation, broken/looping-link controls, and regression proof that direct-root boardctl behavior is unchanged.", "capability_tags": [], "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "9420c62", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "umbrella command: read-only unified view over symlinked sub-repo boards (.coding-hermes/links/<repo> registry); repo-qualified ids, ambiguity warned, broken/loop/out-of-repo links reported, alias dedupe, --list/